                WING COMMANDER II CONFIGURATION INFORMATION
1) Without the Speech Accessory Pack, there is only one place you'll get
speech in WC2: the first scene of the introduction, where the Emperor and
Prince Thrakhath discuss their plans for conquering Humanity. Since the
speech requires 64K of EMS, plus an extra 4K of base memory, you'll
probably want to go back to the INSTALL program and disable the speech
once you've seen the introduction.

2) If you have the minimum memory amount (583,000 bytes), you'll only
get the basic game features. As your free RAM increases, you get more
and more "extras", as follows:
   a. If you have selected speech, 4000 bytes are allocated for that.
   b. If you don't have EMS but do have 20,000 bytes beyond the minimum,
      that memory gets allocated for music.
   c. Last, you get extra spaceflight graphics: planets, the jump flash,
      the larger explosions, debris and cockpit damage.

3) If you have EMS, refer to your documentation for the order in which
the EMS features are enabled. In particular, note that if you only have
a little (100K or less) of free EMS, you can have either speech or
instant replay, but not both.

4) Please remember that, in all cases except sound, music and speech,
features are loaded in on a case-by-case basis. That is, the particular
features you get may change from mission to mission as your memory
allocation changes.

5) We have extensively playtested WC2 under MS-DOS 5.0, and recommend it
highly. You should be able to get 583,000 bytes free on a machine running
MS-DOS 4.01, and we've taken care to make the game run well in that
configuration, but upgrading to 5.0 will increase not only your
free RAM but also your enjoyment of Wing Commander II! Contact the dealer
from whom you purchased this game to find out more about MS-DOS 5.0.


                             ENJOY YOUR GAME!


